{
  "text": " At the hurdle, Kiva and Prue were on the far side. Kiva did not remember going there. She remembered Prue saying, Row and hurdle, and her embers bound, and the hazel going under her and turning. They put up their forearms crossed at the wrists, both of them, and the commodore came over the hazel into the crooks of their arms. Over three to seven, down four to four. The graving did not make the warm sound. It made the other sound, the one it had made on Friday, when somebody shouted elbows, somebody shouted it again, and then somebody else shouted finch, which nobody had ever shouted in the graving before, and Prue went scarlet from her collar to her hair, and did not look up from the commodore on her arms. The graving did not only do anything backup. Forienda",
